Getting the seed right for the game levels is not the killer problem;
that's easy; you just store the shared initial seed, and before laying
out, say, level 11, you take the initial seed and iterate the random
number generator on it k*11 times (where k is some small number
sufficient to prevent you seeing the same stream of random monsters on
each level), and use that number as the seed to lay out level 11.

The _killer_ problem is that you can't allow bones levels unless you
send your _preplay_ bones files along with the seed, and you've probably
long ago modified them by the time you decide that this game is one you
want to put up as a challenge to others.

Without bones files, nethack is a lot less of a game.

More than that, the idea is unworkable anyway; how do you compare your
game where you race for the wizard to win the game with my game where
I've sat on level 4 for 100,000 moves accumulating every artifact and
blessing available from the gods to a neutral player, even if we _did_
happen to start with the same random number seed?

